The IDE that I used was the Kali-built-in Suricata.

Suricata can be installed with: sudo apt update && sudo apt install suricata -y
To update the rules that Suricata uses to scan: sudo suricata-update
This runs Suricata on eth0, which is what Suricata is scanning: sudo suricata -i eth0 -l /var/log/suricata/ --pidfile /var/run/suricata.pid -D
These are the tests run to investigate the IDE: 
  sudo ping -f -c 1000 8.8.8.8
  sudo nmap -sS -p 1-1000 127.0.0.1
  sudo nmap -O 127.0.0.1
  curl "http://testphp.vulnweb.com/artists.php?artist=1%27%20OR%20%271%27%3D%271"
